ifiable thing I can do is record the dnsproxy memory issue as static-only with appropriate confidence, IF I establish the structure bounds. The structure is ~6200 bytes. Writing decoded name (max ~512 bytes from the 0x200 receive buffer) into offset 0 is safe. So dnsproxy name decode is probably NOT exploitable as overflow.\n\nLet me instead verify whether httpd can be traced with a proper argv approach. httpd failed \"firmware version check\" so no.\n\nI think the best remaining move: examine the libavformat ff_rtsp_connect for a truly reachable overflow, or examine another network","stream":true,"block":0}

